    "description": "In this field campaign 59 samples of volcanic and subvolcanic rocks were\ncollected.  Ten of these samples  were analyzed via ICP at the Department of\nGeology, U. de Chile. The samples are subalkaline rocks ranging in composition\nbetween basalt and rhyolite, with a predominance of basaltic to\n\"basaltic-andesitic\" magnetism with transitional affinities between tholeitic\nand calcalkine. The rocks show a high degree of fractionation and  high rates\nof partial fusion, indicating origin in an island arc tectonic  setting. The\nmagnetism of the arc probably occurred during the early  Cretaceous to the\nearly Tertiary.",
